{"data":{"id":"10.48550/arxiv.2604.26952","type":"dois","attributes":{"doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2604.26952","prefix":"10.48550","suffix":"arxiv.2604.26952","identifiers":[{"identifier":"2604.26952","identifierType":"arXiv"}],"alternateIdentifiers":[{"alternateIdentifierType":"arXiv","alternateIdentifier":"2604.26952"}],"creators":[{"name":"Koliogiannis, P. S.","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"P. S.","familyName":"Koliogiannis","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Paar, N.","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"N.","familyName":"Paar","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]}],"titles":[{"title":"Outer-crust equations of state for neutron stars"}],"publisher":"arXiv","container":{},"publicationYear":2026,"subjects":[{"lang":"en","subject":"Nuclear Theory (nucl-th)","subjectScheme":"arXiv"},{"lang":"en","subject":"High Energy Astrophysical Phenomena (astro-ph.HE)","subjectScheme":"arXiv"},{"lang":"en","subject":"Solar and Stellar Astrophysics (astro-ph.SR)","subjectScheme":"arXiv"},{"subject":"FOS: Physical sciences","subjectScheme":"Fields of Science and Technology (FOS)"}],"contributors":[],"dates":[{"date":"2026-04-29T17:59:31Z","dateType":"Submitted","dateInformation":"v1"},{"date":"2026-04-30T01:03:52Z","dateType":"Updated","dateInformation":"v1"},{"date":"2026-05-11T16:40:55Z","dateType":"Submitted","dateInformation":"v2"},{"date":"2026-05-12T02:28:15Z","dateType":"Updated","dateInformation":"v2"},{"date":"2026-08-26T11:47:13Z","dateType":"Submitted","dateInformation":"v3"},{"date":"2026-10-01T01:23:41Z","dateType":"Updated","dateInformation":"v3"},{"date":"2026-04","dateType":"Available","dateInformation":"v1"}],"language":null,"types":{"ris":"GEN","bibtex":"misc","citeproc":"article","schemaOrg":"CreativeWork","resourceType":"Article","resourceTypeGeneral":"Preprint"},"relatedIdentifiers":[{"relationType":"IsVersionOf","relatedIdentifier":"10.1051/0004-6361/202660879","relatedIdentifierType":"DOI"}],"relatedItems":[],"sizes":[],"formats":[],"version":"3","rightsList":[{"rights":"Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International","rightsUri":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode","schemeUri":"https://spdx.org/licenses/","rightsIdentifier":"cc-by-4.0","rightsIdentifierScheme":"SPDX"}],"descriptions":[{"description":"The equation of state of the outer crust of neutron stars is sensitive to nuclear mass predictions and provides a direct connection to the properties of nuclei throughout the nuclide map, including those beyond experimental reach. We quantify the impact of contemporary nuclear mass models on the composition and thermodynamic properties of the outer crust and assess the consequences for crust-dominated neutron-star configurations near the minimum-mass limit. We constructed four outer-crust equations of state based on the relativistic energy density functional and machine-learning mass model tables. The equilibrium composition of cold catalysed matter in $β$-equilibrium was obtained by minimising the Gibbs free energy per nucleon, and the resulting equations of state were implemented in neutron-star structure calculations. The different mass inputs lead to variations in the equilibrium nuclide sequence, distinct last bound nuclei, and moderate shifts in the neutron-drip density. In contrast, the associated thermodynamic properties, as well as the minimum-mass neutron-star configurations, remain closely aligned across the four outer-crust equations of state. The model dependence of the outer crust is primarily reflected in the detailed nuclide composition and in the precise location of neutron drip. Nevertheless, the considered outer-crust equations of state yield closely consistent predictions for the relevant neutron-star observables, providing a reliable input for stellar modelling.","descriptionType":"Abstract"},{"description":"v1: 9 pages, 6 figures, 3 tables; v2: 9 pages, 6 figures, 3 tables, updated text and references; v3: 8 pages, 7 figures, 3 tables; accepted for publication in Astronomy \u0026amp; Astrophysics","descriptionType":"Other"}],"geoLocations":[],"fundingReferences":[],"xml":"","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.26952","contentUrl":null,"metadataVersion":3,"schemaVersion":"http://datacite.org/schema/kernel-4","source":"mds","isActive":true,"state":"findable","reason":null,"viewCount":0,"viewsOverTime":[],"downloadCount":0,"downloadsOverTime":[],"referenceCount":0,"citationCount":0,"citationsOverTime":[],"partCount":0,"partOfCount":0,"versionCount":0,"versionOfCount":1,"created":"2026-04-30T02:11:30.000Z","registered":"2026-04-30T02:11:31.000Z","published":"2026","updated":"2026-10-01T03:50:57.000Z"},"relationships":{"client":{"data":{"id":"arxiv.content","type":"clients"}},"provider":{"data":{"id":"arxiv","type":"providers"}},"media":{"data":{"id":"10.48550/arxiv.2604.26952","type":"media"}},"references":{"data":[]},"citations":{"data":[]},"parts":{"data":[]},"partOf":{"data":[]},"versions":{"data":[]},"versionOf":{"data":[{"id":"10.1051/0004-6361/202660879","type":"dois"}]}}}}